## 3. Drift Audit (measured 2026-08-10)

### 3.1 CRITICAL — OIR content has FOUR different paths across four consumers

| Consumer | Path | Source |
|---|---|---|
| KMP (authoritative) | `test_content/oir/batches` | `GitLiveOIRQuestionCacheManager.kt:52-54` |
| Web | `test_content/oir/question_batches` | `ContentRepository.ts:98` |
| Functions (primary) | `content_oir` | `functions/src/oirScoring.js:41` |
| Functions (fallback) | `oir_batches` | `functions/src/oirScoring.js:43` |

**This is a live correctness risk, not just untidiness.** `oirScoring.js` is the
server-side authority for OIR marks (Tier 2). It reads a collection that *no client
writes and no ingestion script targets*. Scoring is silently dependent on a fallback
chain into a legacy collection. **Fix this first, before any refactor** — Phase 0a.

### 3.2 Firestore path drift, all consumers

| Concern | KMP (authoritative) | Web | Functions |
|---|---|---|---|
| OIR batches | `test_content/oir/batches` | ❌ `…/question_batches` | ❌ `content_oir` → `oir_batches` |
| PPDT | `test_content/ppdt/image_batches` | ✅ same | — |
| TAT | `test_content/tat/image_batches` | ✅ same | — |
| WAT | `test_content/wat/word_batches` | ✅ same | — |
| SRT | `test_content/srt/situation_batches` | ✅ same | — |
| Study materials | `study_materials` | ⚠️ + `studyMaterials` fallback | — |
| GTO tasks | `test_content/gto/task_batches` | ⚠️ absent | — |
| GPE scenarios | `test_content/gto/scenarios/gpe/batches` | ⚠️ absent | — |
| OIR content version | `test_content/oir/meta/config` | ⚠️ absent (no cache invalidation) | — |
| Interview | `interview_sessions` / `_responses` | — | ✅ match |
| Users | `users` | — | ✅ match |

**Orphaned web-only collections** to delete: `studyMaterials`, `ppdtContexts`,
`tatSets`, `watBatches`, `srtBatches`, `oirQuestions`.
**Legitimately server-only** (leave alone): `payments`, `webhook_logs`.

**Duplication inside KMP itself:** `"submissions"` is declared as a `const val` in
three separate files (`COLLECTION_SUBMISSIONS`, `GTO_COLLECTION_SUBMISSIONS`,
`PSYCH_SUBMISSIONS_COLLECTION`, `SUBMISSIONS_COLLECTION`). Even the authoritative
platform has no internal SSOT for paths.

### 3.3 Guess-and-fallback chains (all get deleted)

- OIR (web): `batch_001` → `batch_0` → `batch_pdf_001`
- PPDT (web): caller id → `batch_001` → `ppdt_1`
- Study materials (web): `study_materials` → `studyMaterials`
- `getAvailableBatches` (web): falls back to a hardcoded `defaultsMap` of **fictional
  batches that do not exist in Firestore**
- OIR scoring (functions): `content_oir` → `oir_batches`

Every fallback makes the true contract less knowable and converts a loud failure
into a silent wrong answer. They are the symptom of the missing Tier-1 artifact.

### 3.4 CRITICAL — The OLQ taxonomy has forked on the wire

The 15 Officer-Like Qualities are defined independently in three places:

| Consumer | Location | Casing | 5th OLQ |
|---|---|---|---|
| KMP | `shared/…/domain/model/interview/OLQ.kt` | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` | `SOCIAL_ADJUSTMENT` |
| Functions (Gemini prompt) | `functions/src/olqDefinitions.js` | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` | `SOCIAL_ADJUSTMENT` |
| Web | `components/practice/OLQFactorRadarSVG.tsx` | `camelCase` | ❌ `socialAdaptability` |

Web uses a **different name and a different casing convention** for wire data
produced by the AI evaluation function. Any OLQ the web dossier reads by key is at
risk of rendering as zero/undefined rather than failing loudly. The OLQ set is also
the product's core scoring vocabulary — it is exactly the thing that must never fork.

### 3.5 The subscription model has already forked (highest business severity)

| | KMP | Web |
|---|---|---|
| Tier vocabulary | `FREE`/`PRO`/`PREMIUM` (`SubscriptionTier`) | `'cadet'`/`'officer'`/`'command'` (`AccessTier`) |
| Access model | **monthly quota per test type** (`SubscriptionLimits`, `-1` = unlimited) | **binary gate per test** (`requiredTier`) |
| Real tier source | Firestore `users/{uid}/data/subscription` | `authService.getCurrentUser()?.isPaidMember` — a **boolean**, collapsing 3 tiers to 2 |
| Dev override | Developer Settings, four-way, both platforms | `localStorage` `ssbmax_dev_tier_override`, three-way |
| Usage counters | `SubscriptionUsageDto`, 9 per-test counters | none |

These are two different products, not two spellings. A `PRO` user with 3 of 5 OIR
tests consumed is a state web cannot express. This gates revenue — Phase 4.

**Secondary smell:** `SubscriptionLimits` keys its map on display strings
(`"OIR Tests"`, `"Self Description"`). A typo is a silent miss and it cannot be
generated cleanly. Phase 3 rekeys it on the `TestType` enum.

### 3.6 Contract tests cannot currently catch drift

`web/tests/unit/contracts/firestoreSchemaContract.test.ts` mocks
`firebase/firestore` and asserts **web's own** paths — so it *locks in* the wrong
OIR path rather than detecting it. A per-platform contract test can never detect
cross-platform drift. Structural gap, not a missing assertion. Phase 6.

