## 5. Standing Rules for Every Phase

Applies to all phases below. A phase is **not complete** until every line is true.

1. **Green build, always.** No phase ends with a failing build on any of the four
   consumers. Never start phase N+1 on a red phase N.
2. **TDD.** Tests are written before or alongside implementation. 100% pass — a
   skipped or `.only`'d test counts as a failure (root Rule 12).
3. **Architecture.** MVVM, SOLID, DRY, SSOT upheld. No file over 300 LOC unless SRP
   demands it *and* a comment states why it must not be split (see §4.2).
4. **Resources.** Zero hardcoded strings or colors. KMP → `Res.string` / `MaterialTheme`;
   web → `constants/strings/` + `constants/colors.ts`.
5. **Security.** Every phase re-runs `scripts/validate-security.sh`. No secret ever
   leaves `functions/`. Anti-cheat invariants (web CLAUDE.md §Anti-Cheating) are
   never weakened. Firestore rules are tightened, never loosened.
6. **Tech-debt sweep.** The phase is done only when the task is DONE *and* debt
   incurred during it is REMOVED. Non-negotiable.

### Per-phase verification commands

```bash
./gradlew check                      # KMP: lint + detekt + unit tests (Android + iOS + JVM)
cd web && npm run build && npm test  # Web: tsc strict build + vitest
cd functions && npm test             # Functions
firebase emulators:exec --only firestore "npm --prefix firestore-tests test"
./scripts/validate-security.sh       # 10-point security audit
```

### Phase Handoff Protocol (mandatory, verbatim template)

At the end of every phase, pause and produce:

```
## Phase N Handoff

### 1. Tech debt incurred
- <item> — <where> — <why it arose>

### 2. How it was resolved (immediately, not deferred)
- <item> → <exact steps taken>

### 3. Build & test confirmation
- ./gradlew check .................. PASS/FAIL
- web: npm run build && npm test ... PASS/FAIL  (N tests)
- functions: npm test ............... PASS/FAIL  (N tests)
- emulator rules suite .............. PASS/FAIL  (N tests)
- scripts/validate-security.sh ...... PASS/FAIL  (10/10)

### 4. Contract changes shipped this phase
- <contract file> : <old> → <new> : <compat strategy per §4.1>

### 5. Accepted divergences (if any)
- <platform> differs because <reason>
```

Only after all debt is resolved and every line reads PASS do we start the next phase.

